       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the total daily dose is too high. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day. The usual maximum for a 70 kg adult with normal liver function is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. At 6 g/day there is a real risk of hepatotoxicity.\n\nHere are some options that stay within the limit:\n- **1000 mg PO every 8 hours (3 g/day).** This is a common, conservative choice.\n- **1000 mg PO every 6 hours (4 g/day).** This is the standard maximum.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours (2.6 g/day).** This is another standard regimen.\n\nDid you mean 1000 mg rather than 2000 mg, or 2000 mg once or twice a day? If you tell me the dose and frequency you want, I'll enter it right away. You may also want to run the dose past your resident or attending first."
